        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Single -V / --version from addopts no longer prints version; runs tests instead",
        "explanation": "The hook used to handle `config.option.version > 0`. Now it only handles `> 1`, on the assumption that a single `--version` is caught early in `Config.main()`. That early check (per the comment) inspects the raw args for the literal `--version` string. Paths that give `option.version == 1` without that literal string never reach any version handling: the short form `-V`, `--version` supplied via PYTEST_ADDOPTS or ini `addopts`, and Config objects not created through `main()`. pytest_cmdline_main then returns None and pytest goes on to collect and run the whole test session instead of printing the version and exiting 0. Mixed forms such as `--version -V` are also misclassified as the short output by a literal-count check.",
        "suggestion": "Keep a fallback in the hook: `if config.option.version > 1: show_version_verbose(config); return ExitCode.OK` followed by `elif config.option.version == 1: sys.stdout.write(f\"pytest {pytest.__version__}\\n\"); return ExitCode.OK`. Alternatively, make the early check in `main()` also recognise `-V` and count both spellings.",
        "evidence": "    if config.option.version > 1:",
        "confidence": 0.65,
        "id": "5d479cd85a8f",
